OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, TUC General Secrerary Norman Willis
OL,6, has said the tide is running in favour
OL,7, of trade unions.
OL,9,FSpeaking as delegates gathered in
OL,10,FBlackpool for the Trades Union Congress
OL,11,Fwhich begins tomorrow, Mr Willis said
OL,12,Fthe unions were in confident mood.
OL,14,FHe said he was encouraged by recent
OL,15,Fopinion polls showing that more people
OL,16,Fblame management than the unions for
OL,17,FBritain's economic problems.
OL,19,FBut despite this, he said, the unions
OL,20,Fstill felt under attack from the
OL,21,FGovernment and employers.
OL,23,T]CFrom 03-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
